===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|chĭn}}, {{IPA|en|/t͡ʃɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-chin.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪn|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|chyn}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ċinn||chin}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*kinnuz||chin}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*ǵénus||chin, jaw}}. Compare West Frisian/Dutch {{m|nl|kin}}, Low German/German {{m|de|Kinn}}, {{cog|da|kind}}, {{cog|is|kinn}}, {{cog|cy|gen}}, {{cog|la|gena}}, {{cog|xto|śanwem}}, {{cog|grc|sc=polytonic|γένυς||jaw}}, {{cog|hy|ծնոտ|sc=Armn}}, {{cog|fa|چانه|tr=čâne}}, {{cog|sa|हनु|tr=hánu}}. {{doublet|en|gena}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# The [[bottom]] of a [[face]], {{label|en|specifically}} the [[typically]] [[jutting]] [[jawline]] below the [[mouth]].
# {{lb|en|slang|US}} [[talk|Talk]].
# {{lb|en|slang|British}} A [[lie]], a [[falsehood]].
# {{lb|en|slang|British}} A person of the [[upper class]].
# {{lb|en|boxing|uncountable}} The [[ability]] to [[withstand]] being [[punch]]ed in the [[#chin|chin]] without being [[knock out|knocked out]].
# {{lb|en|aviation}} The lower part of the front of an aircraft, below the [[nose]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|1990|||Army|volume=40|passage=In the cleft of the aircraft's '''chin''' is a small turret for a forward-looking infrared (FLIR) "eyeball" that will enable MH-47E pilots to see clearly in complete darkness {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|2001|||Aviation Week & Space Technology|passage=Lockheed Martin's system is mounted behind a transparent, low-observable window blended into the aircraft's '''chin'''.}}
# The bottom part of a [[mobile phone]], below the [[screen]].

